From 3834d5de1bae114412d4a9f436c00515c5e30868 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:18:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(alerts): a retried finish refusal closes when its
 terminal receipt settles

Tournament.atomic_finish_refused / _outcome_unknown were never closed when
the engine's retry of fn_complete_tournament_terminal committed, so every one
read as an unpaid winner until a manual pass or one-off migration closed it
(15,426 on 2026-09-25, five more passes through 2026-09-27). The passes
stopped after 2026-09-27 16:47 UTC and the backlog grew back: on 2026-10-01
at 15:10 UTC 374 were open, 372 of them on COMPLETED tournaments whose
terminal receipt names the alert's winner and whose payouts equal the
receipt and are paid; the other 2 were RUNNING with no receipt yet.

Adds class 5 to fn_resolve_settled_financial_alerts (cron
ca-resolve-settled-alerts-20m): close only when the tournament is COMPLETED,
its tournament_terminal_settlements receipt exists with winner_id equal to
the alert's context.winner_id, and its payout rows equal the receipt's cash
payouts and are all paid; the proof is repeated under the UPDATE. Guarded
source-only migration with exact pre/post md5 and readback.

Regression: scripts/ci/test-finish-refusal-alert-closer-postgres.py runs the
real preimage (--baseline fails) and the migration (passes) in an isolated
PostgreSQL; wired into CI shard 4 and the change classifier. The CI
baseline counts only when it fails with the exact defect message, so an
infrastructure or fixture error cannot pass the gate.

Rebuilt on main 2a8ac77c1: migration version re-reserved by
scripts/new-migration.mjs (20261001151637), and every pin binding ci.yml
and the classifier restamped from main's bytes with audit records;
verify-source-bindings.py passes (794 pins).

Production Alerts Fleet, incident tournament-finish-refusal-alerts-never-close.

